EXT. SLED-DOG CHECKPOINT - ALASKAN WILDERNESS - DAWN

A log cabin half-buried in drift. Sled dogs asleep in curled rows. Smoke rises from a chimney. Race flags snap in a thin wind.

MUSHER HALVARD OKONKWO-REID, thirties, sits on his sled, dog booties in his lap. Beside him, VET IMELDA TORRES-BAIRD, fifties, listens to a husky's chest with a stethoscope. Official GRAHAM FELLOWES, sixties, stands at the checkpoint with a clipboard.

GRAHAM
You're twelve minutes ahead.

HALVARD
That's good.

GRAHAM
That's very good.

IMELDA
He's sound. Lungs are clear.

HALVARD
Thank you.

IMELDA
She's your lead dog?

HALVARD
Aurora. Eight years.

IMELDA
She's tired.

HALVARD
She's always tired. She never shows it.

A radio on Graham's belt hisses.

RACE CONTROL (V.O.)
(over radio)
Checkpoint Four, Race Control. Be advised: Musher Delacroix is withdrawn. Repeat, withdrawn.

GRAHAM
Copy.

HALVARD
Delacroix? He was my main rival.

GRAHAM
Was.

HALVARD
What happened?

GRAHAM
His team went through the ice.

Silence. Halvard lowers the booties. Imelda lifts her stethoscope from Aurora's chest.

IMELDA
Oh, no.

HALVARD
Is he--

GRAHAM
Alive. Frostbite. Two dogs lost.

HALVARD
I'm sorry.

GRAHAM
You can go.

HALVARD
I think I should stop.

GRAHAM
Now?

IMELDA ^
Now?

HALVARD
If the ice is bad ahead--

GRAHAM
It's not bad. He cut a corner. He was in a hurry.

Halvard stares at Aurora. Aurora stares at him. She yawns. Slowly he laces the booties.

HALVARD
Then I won't be in a hurry.

He rises and calls the team. One by one the huskies stand and shake out their coats. The sled creaks. Halvard steps onto the runners.

HALVARD (CONT'D)
(softly)
Hike.
